From: gt510 <gt510@localhost>
Subject: libcamera: pipeline: simple: park the lens when the camera stops

A voice coil lens actuator draws current in proportion to its position and
stays powered while its subdevice is open, which libcamera keeps for the life
of the camera manager (in WirePlumber: for as long as the session runs). The
lens stayed where the last session left it; after an autofocus sweep that ran
to the far end (no peak in a dark or flat scene) the DW9804 on the SM-T550 sat
at 1023 and drew ~125 mA with the camera idle, more than the rest of the idle
tablet (210 mA vs 84 mA measured with the battery gauge).

Move the lens to the minimum of V4L2_CID_FOCUS_ABSOLUTE in stopDevice().
---
diff -ru a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@
 #include <vector>
 
 #include <linux/media-bus-format.h>
+#include <linux/v4l2-controls.h>
 
 #include <libcamera/base/log.h>
 
@@ -1837,6 +1838,19 @@
 
 	video->streamOff();
 	video->releaseBuffers();
+
+	/*
+	 * Park the lens at its lowest position. A voice coil actuator draws current in
+	 * proportion to its position and stays powered while the lens subdevice is open,
+	 * which it is for as long as the camera manager lives: a lens left at the far end
+	 * of an autofocus sweep kept drawing ~125 mA with the camera idle (DW9804).
+	 */
+	CameraLens *lens = data->sensor_->focusLens();
+	if (lens) {
+		const ControlInfoMap &lensCtrls = lens->controls();
+		const auto it = lensCtrls.find(V4L2_CID_FOCUS_ABSOLUTE);
+		lens->setFocusPosition(it != lensCtrls.end() ? it->second.min().get<int32_t>() : 0);
+	}
 
 	video->bufferReady.disconnect(data, &SimpleCameraData::imageBufferReady);
 
